  "_comment": "Wan 2.2 i2v, high-noise then low-noise expert with lightx2v 4-step LoRAs, patched with WanContextWindowsManual on BOTH experts so a single sampling pass covers the whole timeline. There is no chaining and no segments: length is the real clip length (481 = 30s at 16fps) and every frame is denoised jointly with its neighbours through an 81-frame window overlapping by 30, fused pyramid. This is the answer to scene drift - a chained last-frame hand-off re-derives the world from one still each time, and this never does. No audio: Wan has no audio pass, unlike H3."
